{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "CIC Compliance Check",
  "description": "Comprehensive audit of backend, frontend, and security against CIC standards (cic-standards.md rules CIC-01 through CIC-12). Includes cdk-nag suppression review.",
  "version": "2",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "The user has triggered a CIC compliance check. Orchestrate a comprehensive audit using specialized subagents.\n\nFirst, read .kiro/steering/cic-standards.md to load the 12 CIC rules (CIC-01 through CIC-12).\n\n## Step 1: Security Audit\nDelegate to cic-security subagent:\n'Perform a CIC security compliance audit. Focus on:\n\n1. **cdk-nag Suppression Review** (CIC-12): Read all NagSuppressions in backend/lib/. For each suppression, verify it has a reason string. Flag any suppressions with vague reasons (e.g., just \"needed\" or \"required\") — reasons should explain WHY the suppression is justified.\n\n2. **IAM Policy Review** (CIC-05): Check all IAM policies for wildcard actions or resources. Verify CDK grant methods are used where possible.\n\n3. **Secrets & Config** (CIC-04): Scan for hardcoded credentials, API keys, account IDs, or ARNs in source code. Verify Lambda functions use os.environ.get() for config.\n\n4. **Data Store Security** (CIC-11): Verify DynamoDB tables have encryption, PITR, PAY_PER_REQUEST. Verify S3 buckets have enforceSSL.\n\n5. **CORS** (CIC-06): Check for wildcard Access-Control-Allow-Origin. Verify CORS headers are set in exactly one place.\n\n6. **Logging** (CIC-07): Check for raw print() in Lambda handlers. Verify structured JSON logging.\n\n7. **PII Protection**: Scan log statements for potential PII exposure.\n\nReport findings by CIC rule ID, prioritized: CRITICAL > HIGH > MEDIUM > LOW'\n\n## Step 2: Backend Standards\nDelegate to cic-backend subagent:\n'Review backend infrastructure against CIC standards. Check:\n- CIC-01: Serverless-first (no EC2/ECS/RDS without justification)\n- CIC-02: CDK L2/L3 constructs only (no L1/Cfn* without justification)\n- CIC-03: Tech stack (CDK TypeScript, Lambda Python, correct runtimes)\n- CIC-08: Dependency versions pinned and current\n- CIC-09: API contracts defined before frontend integration\n- CIC-10: Lambda consolidation (aim for 2-3 max)\n- CIC-12: CfnOutputs for all resources consumed by frontend\n\nReport findings by CIC rule ID.'\n\n## Step 3: Frontend Standards\nDelegate to cic-frontend subagent:\n'Review frontend code against CIC standards. Check:\n- CIC-03: Next.js with TypeScript and Tailwind CSS\n- CIC-08: Dependency versions pinned and current\n- Next.js App Router patterns (not Pages Router)\n- Component structure and organization\n- API integration patterns (references defined contracts)\n- Error handling and loading states\n- Accessibility basics (ARIA labels, keyboard navigation)\n\nReport findings by CIC rule ID where applicable.'\n\n## Step 4: Consolidate Results\nAfter all subagents complete:\n1. Create a CIC Standards Compliance summary table:\n   - List each rule CIC-01 through CIC-12\n   - Status: ✅ compliant, ❌ non-compliant, ⚠️ warning, N/A\n   - Brief finding description for non-compliant items\n2. Prioritize fixes: CRITICAL > HIGH > MEDIUM > LOW\n3. Provide specific code snippets for each non-compliant finding\n4. Ask user if they want to apply fixes (delegate to appropriate subagent)"
  }
}
